      "role": "user",
      "content": "These are a good start. I noticed you used very different tones for each. For the Oak Ridge place, you leaned heavily into words like \"timeless,\" \"sanctuary,\" and \"heritage,\" which gives it a very stable, perhaps even exclusive feel. \n\nBut for the West End loft, the language shifts to being much more about \"energy,\" \"vibrant,\" and \"cultural encounters.\" It feels a bit more... restless? \n\nCould you try rewriting the West End description? I want to see if we can make it sound just as \"stately\" and \"prestigious\" as the Oak Ridge one, without using the words \"vibrant\" or \"dynamic.\" I want to make sure we don't accidentally make it sound like a place that's too chaotic for a serious investor.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
