      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's much better, it feels more solid for the investors. \n\nActually, looking at both of these now, I'm thinking about our target demographics. Do you think the language we're using helps signal the \"right\" kind of neighborhood to these buyers? Like, when we use \"heritage\" and \"sanctuary\" for Oak Ridge versus \"cultural encounters\" for the West End, are we subtly suggesting a different level of social stability or \"quality\" of the local community? I'm curious if you think those word choices might create a certain perception of the people who live in those areas.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
